    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0275" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg157"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Anderson to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 18, 1889</date>.
                        (Received July 30.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 315.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 313, dated
                    July 15, I have the honor to report that I have this day mailed to Sir Edmund
                    Monson, at Athens, a note of which I inclose a copy and in which I acknowledge
                    the receipt of his letter of July 8, and thank him for accepting the task of
                    arbitration referred to him by the treaty anent the Carlos Butterfield
                    claim.</p>
                <p>An identic note of acknowledgment and thanks has been sent to Sir Edmund by the
                    Royal Danish minister for foreign affairs.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. B. Anderson</hi>.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d117-a1.xml" xpointer="d117-a1"/>
            </div>
